$DIR/test.p:11:11: cannot use File as owner in Box: File is an owner and owner does not allow owners
    Inside the generic code, values of owner are copied freely. Copying an owner
    would leave several values that all free the same memory.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    If the generic code moves each value of owner at most once, allow owners in
    its declaration:
        [owner owner any]
    Otherwise use copies made explicitly with Clone, or pointers to the owners.
    (see "Owner types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.18)
    (run "pluto explain E3207" for a longer explanation)
